1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
The Story That Was Passed On. In a quiet
Ethiopian village, an elderly man...

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:17,000
One evening, as the sun set, the child
asked him a question.

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Grandfather, why do you always tell us
the same old stories?

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:30,000
The elder smiled, and began telling a
story about their village.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Years ago, a harsh dry season came to
the land, and people began to worry.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Yet one child shared the little food
they had with a struggling neighbour.

7
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:53,000
In return, the neighbour gave the child
a single seed saved for planting.

8
00:00:53,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Together, the village planted that seed,
watered it, and watched it grow.

9
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:08,000
My child, what matters is not when a
story happened, but what it teaches us.

10
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:16,000
And so the lesson lived on: when a story
is passed on, a generation carries it...

